      <p>Cat Ilacad didn't start out as a business mentor. She started as a business owner. In the early 2000s, she founded <strong>Posh Nails</strong> — a nail salon she grew from a single location into a recognized brand built entirely on her own drive, instincts, and relentless work ethic.</p>
      <p>For years, everything depended on her. Every decision, every client, every operational detail flowed through Cat alone. The business grew — but so did the pressure. <strong>She was running her business. Her business was not running without her.</strong></p>
      <p>The turning point came when she stopped asking "how do I work harder?" and started asking "how do I build something that works?" What followed was a deliberate, years-long process of building four foundational systems that transformed Posh Nails from a business that needed her — to a business that could lead itself.</p>
      <p>That experience became the foundation for everything Cat teaches today through the <strong>CEO Systems Method</strong>.</p>
